The liability cap in Section 8.3 of the Vertex Master Services Agreement (MSA-2026-022) is as follows:

* The aggregate liability of each Party under or in connection with this Agreement shall not exceed five hundred thousand United States dollars (USD 500,000) in aggregate over the life of this Agreement (Section 8.3).
* This liability cap applies to direct losses arising from the breach of this Agreement (Section 8.2).
* The limitations in Sections 8.1 and 8.3 do not apply to certain exclusions, including:
	+ Indemnity obligations under Section 9 (Section 8.4(a));
	+ Breach of Section 5 (Section 8.4(b));
	+ Fraud or wilful misconduct (Section 8.4(c));
	+ Client's obligation to pay fees properly due (Section 8.4(d)).

Note that Section 8.3 is not the same as Section 8.3 in MSA-2026-014 (Northwind), as noted in the Master Services Agreement document.
